# Git branch hygiene

Before any commit, push, or PR in this repo:

## Pre-flight (run in parallel)

```bash
git fetch origin
git status
git branch -vv
gh pr list --head "$(git branch --show-current)" --state all
```

## Rules

1. **One task = one branch** — name by scope: `docs/...`, `fix/...`, `feat/...`. Never append unrelated work to an existing branch.
2. **Check if branch is stale** — if current branch has a merged or open PR for different work, branch from fresh `origin/main` instead.
3. **Start new work from main:**
   ```bash
   git checkout main && git pull origin main
   git checkout -b <scope>/<short-name>
   ```
4. **Before push** — `git log origin/main..HEAD` must contain only commits for the current task. If polluted, cherry-pick onto a fresh branch from `origin/main`.
5. **After PR merge** — delete remote branch; `git checkout main && git pull`.
6. **Verify gh auth** — `gh repo view MalibuAI/malibu` must succeed before push.

## Auto-merge PRs

Once all required CI checks are green, **merge automatically** — do not wait for "merge it" or "ship it".

1. After opening or pushing a PR, poll checks: `gh pr checks <number>`
2. When all required checks pass: `gh pr merge <number> --squash --delete-branch`
3. Sync local: `git checkout main && git pull origin main`

Hold off only if: CI is failing, checks are pending, the user explicitly asked not to merge, or there are unresolved merge conflicts.

## Recovery from wrong branch

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout main && git pull origin main
git checkout -b <scope>/<short-name>
git cherry-pick <clean-commit-sha>
git push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --base main
git push origin --delete <stale-branch>  # if recreated after merge
```
